      "writtenOn": "2024-01-10T22:44:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "FYI wifi usage of `core_platform` [here](https://source.corp.google.com/h/googleplex-android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Wifi/flags/Android.bp;l\u003d45)\n\n\u003e I think doing this here will be okay as long as nothing gets released\n\nThe documentation go/android-flags-howto-apis#new-apis-in-mainline-code tell mainline to use the flag with a string, but this is not convenient at all.\nI am looking for a way (like wifi did) to use the Flag in the framework.\n\nI would be very interested to know what is dangerous since we are already releasing with flags cf go/bt-ts-workflow.\n24Q2 is containing our first released flags within the module (none in framework for now)",
      "parentUuid": "97b6999c_952cb1c2",
